Z||000000||Neal||07-30-2001||01:46 AM||||A couple of weeks ago a friend of mines fiero started making a high pitched squeal,  It sounded like a vacuum leak but LOUD.  It would go away if you gave the car gas but would return when the RPM's stabilized.  After 3 shops looked at it he finally was sent in the right direction, check the fuel injectors, the tip of one was broken off.<BR>He replaced the injectors and the noise is gone bet the car idels at about 3000 rpm.<P>Now after this long explanation, what would make the car idel at 3000 when just faulty injectors were replaced?  the car is an 88GT, ran perfect before and is very well maintained||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||07-30-2001||06:13 AM||||sounds like a vacume leak- easy to get something leaking whilst messing around all those hoses and also check the egr tube.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Neal||07-30-2001||04:19 PM||||A vacume leak is what i have suspected, but i havent seen or heard it yet, i just wanted to collect as much info as possible.<P>And i will definitly check the egr tube.<P>Any more ideas||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTBro||07-30-2001||08:08 PM||||I put my money on the EGR tube.  Could have cracked when the plenum was removed.  Air is rushing into the intake manifold uncontrollably, bypassing the throttle body.<P>BTW...  What did you/he do with the injectors you took out?  I have a clogged one and dont want to pay $380 for a full set.<P>------------------<BR>AOL IM: GTFiero86Dan<BR>'86 GT 4 speed<BR>'87 GT Auto<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87GTBrosig1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Neal||07-30-2001||09:22 PM||||After some investigation we found a big crack in the egr tube.  Got a replacement but it started to rain.  So hopefully we will know if the car runs right tomorrow.<P>And yes both me and my friend have several injectors, $2 each from a pick and pull.||||reg||1
